{"seconds": 45.9, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! I win the queen. The main line is:\n1. **Qh7+** Nxh7\n2. **Bxh7+** Kh8 (or Kg7)\n3. **Nxf7+** Kxh7\n4. **Nxd8** and White has won the queen for a bishop and pawn\u2014a decisive material advantage.\n\n**Best move:** Qh7+\n\n**Main line:** Qh7+ Nxh7 Bxh7+ Kh8 Nxf7+ Kxh7 Nxd8\n\n**Motif:** deflection (the queen sacrifice on h7 forces the knight to h7, which deviates it from defending f7), combined with attraction (the king is lured to h8, a vulnerable square).\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your opponent's king lacks escape squares and you have concentrated attackers nearby, look for forcing sacrifices that redirect defenders. Here, Qh7+ forces the knight to h7, allowing Bxh7+ to strip away the king's shelter. Then Nxf7+ attacks the undefended king, and after Kxh7, Nxd8 wins the queen outright. Always calculate two moves ahead when sacrificing toward an exposed king\u2014the tempo often works in your favor.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qh7+\", \"line\": [\"Qh7+\", \"Nxh7\", \"Bxh7+\", \"Kh8\", \"Nxf7+\", \"Kxh7\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "square": "g8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "square": "h7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "square": "h6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/